<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ōmi Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ōmi Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, corresponding to modern Shiga prefecture, surrounding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-biwa">Lake Biwa</a>. Lying on the main routes from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> to the east and north, it was strategically vital and fought over during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a> by clans such as the Rokkaku, Kyōgoku and Azai. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a> built his Azuchi castle there from 1576.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/omi-province.jpg" alt="Ōmi Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Omi.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
